{
  "Uuid": "fec791fc-0b72-4147-8e9f-415b95c8808a",
  "IsCustomNode": false,
  "Description": "Main pulling calculation and live Excel export, with the existing route inspector and eight additional section-type example code blocks matching the Word diagrams. Example blocks are independent of the route solver. V21.5 adds an HV cable minimum bend radius check (installation and installed), set by two new inputs. V2 adds a grade break tolerance input (default 0.3 deg) so export arc approximations are not counted as kinks. V3 corrects the report title/version label (V21.5) and garbled dash and r-squared characters. V4 removes the word Dynamo from the exported Excel report. V5 adds optional ELEK-style high sidewall friction (friction, threshold) and a three-cable factor rule switch, both off by default. V6 adds an ELEK-style section list sheet (forward and reverse) for each route. V7 defaults follow ELEK: friction 0.45 dropping to 0.2 above 2185 N/m sidewall force, IEEE three-cable factor. V8 allowable tension is 80% of the 28 kN grip limit (22,400 N), the ELEK tension reduction.",
  "Name": "21.5 Civil3D_MWP_PullCal_Linked_Fill_Jamming_Newtons_Fixed_Parabolic_CORRECTED_HELP_V13",
  "ElementResolver": {
    "ResolutionMap": {
      "Math": {
