      {
        "Id": "2a1131b365c04fb792f7f2f2d50cea4f",
        "Title": "6 | Formula inspector (step-by-step check)",
        "DescriptionText": "Pick a route, direction, section and step to see the formulas behind one integration step.\n- Inspect route: Route to inspect (1-based).\n- 01 - Selected calculation data: Cable and section values for the chosen step.\n- 02 - Cable weight, friction and fill: Cable weight W, effective friction f and fill.\n- 03 - Current integration step inputs: Tension, angle, curvature and weight entering the step.\n- 04.1 - RK4 stage k1: RK4 stage k1: rate of tension change (N/m).\n- 04.2 - RK4 stage k2: RK4 stage k2 (N/m).\n- 04.3 - RK4 stage k3: RK4 stage k3 (N/m).\n- 04.4 - RK4 stage k4: RK4 stage k4 (N/m).\n- 05 - Step exit tension and verification: Combines k1 to k4 into the step exit tension and checks it.\n- 06 - Step exit SWBP and verification: Sidewall pressure at the step exit, with check.\n- Inspect direction: Pull direction to inspect: 1 forward, 2 reverse.\n- Inspect section: Section to inspect, in pull order.\n- Inspect integration step: Integration step to inspect inside that section.\n- Code Block: Splits the solver output into data, cable, step, geometry and selection.\n- 07 - Whole section and unknown joint: Whole-section result and unknown joints (grade breaks).\n- 08 - Straight / slope closed-form check: Closed-form hand check for straight and sloped sections.\n- 09 - Level horizontal bend closed-form check: Closed-form hand check for level horizontal bends.",
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
        "Nodes": [
