      {
        "Id": "85067611defc4c1cb4d18e7365ee2599",
        "Title": "4.7 Weight correction factor - IEEE standard (Wc)",
        "DescriptionText": "Project equations and pulling conditions; middle-band IEEE discrepancy is explicitly identified.",
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
        "Nodes": [
          "8109d536444e4bcaafff1f88c72f7060",
          "156a2310a5d541e1a46d60592fdd8d31",
          "9f4111482bfe44488f8161715d7279cc",
          "3e92724789ee4bc797bd1806a2391b4d",
          "3d26d3f792f442109d18be27cbe8d61a",
          "d6abe43d34ea4329b3105a845cc2d745"
        ],
        "HasNestedGroups": false,
        "Left": 3990.0,
        "Top": 10019.6,
        "Width": 2617.6000000000004,
        "Height": 1245.3999999999996,
        "FontSize": 36.0,
        "GroupStyleId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
        "InitialTop": 10092.0,
        "InitialHeight": 995.0,
        "TextblockHeight": 62.4,
        "Background": "#FFA4E1FF"
      },
      {
        "Id": "9f4111482bfe44488f8161715d7279cc",
        "Title": "Wc and effective friction\n\nD = conduit inside diameter; d = cable outside diameter; r=d/(D-d).\nProject rule for THREE cables:\nD/d <= 2.5: Wc=1/sqrt(1-r^2) (Equation 7b reference supplied).\n2.5 < D/d <= 3.0: Wc=1+2r^2 (project-supplied rule).\nD/d > 3.0: Wc=1+(4/3)r^2.\nSingle: Wc=1; two: triangular; four: diamond; more than four: Wc=1.4.\nf prime = Wc*f. The 1.0/2.0/3.0 in the supplied notes are case numbers.\nMixed cable sizes: 1.4 assumption noted, but this graph accepts one cable diameter/mass\nonly.",
        "DescriptionText": null,
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
        "Nodes": [],
        "HasNestedGroups": false,
        "Left": 5200.0,
        "Top": 10100.0,
        "Width": 0.0,
        "Height": 0.0,
        "FontSize": 36.0,
        "GroupStyleId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
        "InitialTop": 0.0,
        "InitialHeight": 0.0,
        "TextblockHeight": 0.0,
        "Background": "#FFC1D676"
      },
      {
        "Id": "3e92724789ee4bc797bd1806a2391b4d",
        "Title": "Expected sidewall pressure\n\nSingle: P=T1/R.\nThree cables maintained in triangular formation: P=(Wc*T1)/(2*R).\nCradled: P=((3*Wc-2)*T1)/(3*R).\nDiamond / fourcables: P=(Wc-1)*T1/R, per supplied MWP graph.\nT1 is local tension at the point assessed. Route Peak SWBP samples tension and curvature\nalong the bend.\nUnits: tension N, radius m, pressure N/m. Positive manufacturer override takes priority.",
        "DescriptionText": null,
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
        "Nodes": [],
        "HasNestedGroups": false,
        "Left": 6300.0,
        "Top": 10100.0,
        "Width": 0.0,
        "Height": 0.0,
        "FontSize": 36.0,
        "GroupStyleId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
        "InitialTop": 0.0,
        "InitialHeight": 0.0,
        "TextblockHeight": 0.0,
        "Background": "#FFC1D676"
      },
      {
        "Id": "3d26d3f792f442109d18be27cbe8d61a",
        "Title": "Three-core pulling method - project supplied\n\nUse only a Triple Stocking for Pulling Three Cable Cores, type K50/3, as specified by the\nproject notes referencing ESBN's MV/LV Installations Standards and Practice Manual.\nDo not use a single stocking encompassing all three cables; the supplied notes warn of\nirreparable cable damage.\nUse tie wraps every 5 m to maintain trefoil throughout the section.\nUse approved lubricant in the quantities specified in manual section 2.7.10.\nThese conditions apply to the three-core case; they do not confirm a 17-cable arrangement.",
        "DescriptionText": null,
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
        "Nodes": [],
        "HasNestedGroups": false,
        "Left": 5200.0,
        "Top": 10950.0,
        "Width": 0.0,
        "Height": 0.0,
        "FontSize": 36.0,
        "GroupStyleId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
        "InitialTop": 0.0,
        "InitialHeight": 0.0,
        "TextblockHeight": 0.0,
        "Background": "#FFC1D676"
      },
      {
        "Id": "d6abe43d34ea4329b3105a845cc2d745",
        "Title": "Source distinction and fill caution\n\nThe project-supplied 2.5<D/d<=3 Wc rule is not verified as IEEE 1185-2019. Verified IEEE\n1185-2010 text uses the cradled expression for three cables in this band and reserves\n1+2r^2 for four cables in diamond.\nReference:\nhttps://ptacts.uspto.gov/ptacts/public-informations/petitions/1554880/download-documents?artifactId=oWdBe7rMg5XtUz8CBriLLzex-cH5o1pjEcuhqW9sE64JX9LEnkXJkHQ\nProject caution: approaching 40% conduit fill increases jamming and damage risk; a\nfill-limit check alone does not establish pull suitability.\nThe 40% NEC statement and ESBN method are supplied project notes, not independently\nverified here.",
        "DescriptionText": null,
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
        "Nodes": [],
        "HasNestedGroups": false,
        "Left": 6300.0,
        "Top": 10950.0,
